{"type":"diagram","design":"M_001","title":"Kroger unified data foundation on GCP","lead":"BigQuery harmonizes real-time store transactions, catalog attributes, and supply chain telemetry.","center":"BigQuery data hub","text":"Centralizing disparate retail data streams into a governed BigQuery repository enables low-latency feature generation across all supermarket locations.","items":[{"title":"Point of sale streams","text":"Pub/Sub streams register checkout events and digital cart transactions from stores.","icon":"cart-tech"},{"title":"Perishable inventory","text":"Dataflow harmonizes on-hand balances, expiration dates, and backroom intake quantities.","icon":"database-refresh"},{"title":"Catalog and pricing","text":"Assortment, markdowns, and promo schedules sync to governed tables.","icon":"price-tag"},{"title":"Warehouse logistics","text":"DC dispatch logs, vendor lead times, and transit schedules feed supply availability views.","icon":"truck"},{"title":"Store floor telemetry","text":"Handheld scans and night-crew restocking logs capture real-time store execution.","icon":"smartphone"},{"title":"External signals","text":"Local weather forecasts, community events, and holidays enrich baseline demand data.","icon":"cloud-signal"}],"notes":"To forecast store demand accurately, Kroger requires a unified data foundation on Google Cloud. Streaming point-of-sale transactions, real-time store assortment, dynamic pricing, and night-crew stocking telemetry are ingested via Pub/Sub and Dataflow directly into BigQuery. This architecture eliminates data silos between merchandising and store operations.

