{"type":"diagram","design":"T_001","title":"Target architecture for enterprise forecasting","lead":"End-to-end Google Cloud architecture connecting BigQuery, Vertex AI, and store execution systems.","layers":[{"title":"Store and associate execution layer","text":"Associate handheld devices, night-crew task queues, and automated ERP purchase order generation interfaces across all retail stores.","icon":"automation"},{"title":"Agentic and predictive intelligence layer","text":"Vertex AI forecasting models paired with Gemini Enterprise grounded in store assortment hierarchies to guide daily fresh orders.","icon":"line chart"},{"title":"Unified data and feature layer","text":"BigQuery enterprise data warehouse and Vertex AI Feature Store managing governed datasets for cross-departmental supply analytics.","icon":"database"},{"title":"Streaming ingestion and integration layer","text":"Pub/Sub messaging and Dataflow stream pipelines capturing POS register scans, ERP updates, and upstream supply chain logistic events.","icon":"message"}],"parts":["Pub/Sub","Dataflow","BigQuery","Vertex AI","Gemini Enterprise","Looker Studio"],"takeaway":"Tightly coupled cloud components eliminate batch latency between customer checkout signals and store replenishment actions.","notes":"The target architecture integrates Kroger store operations with Google Cloud AI services. Streaming ingestion via Pub/Sub and Dataflow feeds BigQuery, which grounds Gemini Enterprise and powers Vertex AI forecasting workflows. Predictions flow directly into associate handheld systems and ERP ordering engines to coordinate night-crew shelf stocking and intake quantities.

