{"type":"cards","design":"S_019","title":"Data governance and real-time observability","lead":"Automated validation and lineage controls protect model integrity across thousands of store feeds.","items":[{"title":"Automated schema validation","text":"Dataflow ingestion pipelines enforce strict schema contracts on incoming POS and inventory streams, routing malformed records to dead-letter queues before they corrupt BigQuery forecasting tables.","icon":"shield-database"},{"title":"End-to-end data lineage","text":"Dataplex tracks field-level lineage from raw store register scans through feature transformations to Vertex AI predictions, giving data engineering teams complete auditability.","icon":"workflow-path"},{"title":"Pipeline freshness monitoring","text":"Automated observability alerts notify operations teams if store inventory syncs or warehouse shipment logs fall behind schedule, preventing stale inputs during daily order windows.","icon":"monitor-wave"},{"title":"Feature drift detection","text":"Vertex AI Model Monitoring continuously compares live store input distributions against training baselines, flagging sudden shifts in promotional pricing or local buying behavior.","icon":"chart-search"}],"notes":"Reliable demand forecasting depends on strict data governance across all retail locations. Automated schema validation in Dataflow, lineage tracking, freshness alerts, and Vertex AI drift detection ensure that corrupted or delayed store telemetry never degrades replenishment recommendations.

