{"type":"bullets","design":"ENGINE_BULLETS","title":"Core integration points with retail IT systems","lead":"Bidirectional APIs synchronize Vertex AI forecasts with Kroger enterprise resource and store platforms.","points":["Enterprise ERP sync: Automated egress pipelines publish approved store-SKU quantities into procurement modules to trigger supplier purchase orders.","Warehouse management sync: Forecasted store volumes feed distribution allocation engines to optimize pallet building and cold-chain routing schedules.","Store ledger updates: Receiving scans, customer returns, and shrink adjustments flow into BigQuery to continuously recalibrate on-hand store balances.","Associate tasking: Vertex AI and Gemini push prioritized restocking alerts and intake quantities to floor devices for night-crew shelf execution.","Pricing engines: Markdown schedules and circular promotional calendars sync bidirectionally to align price elasticity with perishable shelf life."],"callout":{"label":"Closed-loop execution","title":"Smooth store floor coordination","text":"Integrating Vertex AI agentic workflows with existing store systems translates predictive forecasts into structured associate tasks, coordinating night-crew shelf stocking and daily intake quantities without manual spreadsheet exports."},"notes":"Forecasts only reduce food waste when they seamlessly trigger operational action across retail IT systems. Bidirectional pipelines connect BigQuery and Vertex AI with enterprise ERP procurement, warehouse management, and store handheld devices. This expands upon Kroger associate-facing AI systems that coordinate night-crew shelf stocking, intake quantities, and floor task prioritization.

