{"type":"cards","title":"Supply chain cycle time compression benchmarks","lead":"Shifting retail chains from legacy rules to ML demand sensing shortens planning cycles and safeguards shelf availability.","items":[{"title":"Industry benchmark: up to 65% reduction in lost sales from stockouts","text":"AI-driven supply chain planning aligns store intake with localized customer intent, slashing lost sales while lowering overall inventory holding levels. Continuous model evaluation captures regional trends, ensuring distribution centers stage freight efficiently before peak weekend shopping rushes.","icon":"target"},{"title":"Automated replenishment planning speed","text":"Replacing manual spreadsheet adjustments with Vertex AI predictions accelerates store ordering cycles and helps planners react immediately to local demand shifts. Automated pipelines continuously ingest transactional signals, empowering regional coordinators to reallocate merchandise without waiting on batch reports.","icon":"automation"},{"title":"Perishable inventory spoilage reduction","text":"Aligning daily delivery schedules with granular Gemini demand forecasts minimizes backroom holding times and keeps fresh produce moving to grocery shelves. Precise intake pacing prevents perishable spoilage at loading docks while ensuring core staple items remain fully stocked throughout regional promotional events.","icon":"line chart"}],"notes":"Industry research from McKinsey demonstrates why compressing the replenishment cycle is critical for fresh grocery categories. Machine learning demand planning models compress replenishment order cycle times by up to 35% while reducing forecast error rates by up to 50% compared to traditional statistical methods. This responsiveness directly protects store revenue, slashing lost sales from stockouts by up to 65%.

