{"type":"timeline","design":"E_004","title":"Program delivery timeline and key milestones","lead":"A four-phase delivery plan moves from data foundation and pilot validation to full enterprise rollout.","items":[{"date":"Phase 1","title":"Define and data foundation","text":"Conduct virtual workshops to prioritize perishable department requirements, finalize technical solution design, and establish governed BigQuery and Vertex AI Feature Store pipelines for historical POS, loyalty, and shrink data.","icon":"database"},{"date":"Phase 2","title":"Model build and backtesting","text":"Train Vertex AI demand forecasting models and configure Gemini context agents, executing historical backtests against baseline statistical methods to validate error reduction and replenishment cycle speed before store deployment.","icon":"brain-ai"},{"date":"Phase 3","title":"Pilot store cohort launch","text":"Deploy automated order recommendations and handheld associate workflows across selected pilot store tiers, measuring forecast accuracy, perishable waste diversion, and manager planning speed at a formal value checkpoint.","icon":"flask"},{"date":"Phase 4","title":"Enterprise scale and MLOps","text":"Expand validated Vertex AI and Gemini workflows across regional supermarket divisions, transitioning ongoing drift monitoring, automated retraining pipelines, and continuous model optimization to the joint operations team.","icon":"rocket"}],"notes":"Our delivery timeline follows the proven 66degrees methodology of Define, Design, Plan, and Value Checkpoint to de-risk enterprise AI adoption. Phase 1 establishes the BigQuery data foundation and solution design, while Phase 2 validates Vertex AI model performance through rigorous backtesting. Phase 3 introduces a live store pilot with a formal Value Checkpoint before scaling across the broader Kroger store footprint in Phase 4.

