{"type":"process","title":"Current architecture on on-premise VMs","items":[{"title":"Monolithic tracking services on fixed VMs","fix":"Decouple into stateless GKE microservices across isolated node pools for independent scaling.","status":"Amber","icon":"activity","text":"Fix: Decouple into stateless GKE microservices across isolated node pools for independent scaling. This prevents resource contention and isolates failures to specific domains."},{"title":"Single-datacenter routing adds regional latency","fix":"Terminate TCP/TLS at edge Google Front Ends within 1-5 ms of users.","status":"Amber","icon":"analytics","text":"Fix: Terminate TCP/TLS at edge Google Front Ends within 1-5 ms of users. Offloading SSL handshakes near clients drastically cuts latency and saves origin compute capacity."},{"title":"Manual VM provisioning delays traffic scaling","fix":"Enable GKE Horizontal Pod Autoscaler and Cluster Autoscaler for automated burst capacity.","status":"Amber","icon":"maximize","text":"Fix: Enable GKE Horizontal Pod Autoscaler and Cluster Autoscaler for automated burst capacity. Workloads scale pod counts and node counts quickly in response to traffic."},{"title":"Local load balancers lack Global failover","fix":"Deploy Global external Application Load Balancers with automatic cross-region backend failover.","status":"Amber","icon":"security","text":"Fix: Deploy Global external Application Load Balancers with automatic cross-region backend failover. Client traffic routes directly to healthy backends during regional outages."}],"notes":"Northwind Logistics currently runs monolithic shipment tracking services on static on-premise virtual machines, creating single points of failure and regional latency bottlenecks. We resolve these four constraints by migrating to a two-region Google Kubernetes Engine architecture fronted by Global external Application Load Balancers that terminate TLS within 1-5 ms of users.

